    #   STRUCTURAL rather than behavioural, and that is forced, not a preference: a VERBATIM copy behaves
    #   identically, so no fixture can see one. The defect becomes observable only after someone edits one
    #   of the copies - which is after the moment a fixture could have warned about it.
    #   The anchor is READ OUT OF THE LIVE FUNCTION, never restated here: a gate that spelled it out would BE
    #   the next copy and would have to be edited in lockstep with the thing it guards. Both arms judge files
    #   OTHER than this one, so neither can be satisfied by its own declaration - the self-satisfying shape
    #   TD171/TD175 record, and the reason the call channel below is AST rather than grep.
    $haFiles = @('scripts/handoff.ps1', 'scripts/_context.ps1')
    $haAsts = [ordered]@{}
    foreach ($haF in $haFiles) { $haAsts[$haF] = [System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::ParseFile((Join-Path $RepoRoot $haF), [ref]$null, [ref]$null) }
    $haFail = $false
